Solutio is a web3 crowdfunding platform built on top of the ICP blockchain.
# Crypto Rules for Solutio

## General Principles
1. All transactions must be conducted on the Internet Computer Protocol (ICP) blockchain
2. Smart contracts must be audited before deployment
3. All crypto-related operations must be transparent and verifiable on-chain

## Token Standards
1. Use the ICRC-1 standard for fungible tokens
2. Use the ICRC-7 standard for NFTs
3. All token contracts must implement the required interfaces from the ICP standards

## Security Guidelines
1. Private keys must never be stored in plain text
2. Use hardware wallets for high-value transactions
3. Implement multi-signature requirements for treasury operations
4. Regular security audits must be conducted

## Crowdfunding Rules
1. All crowdfunding campaigns must be fully escrowed
2. Funds are only released upon successful completion of milestones
3. Users can withdraw their contributions at any time before milestone completion
4. A minimum threshold must be met before any development work begins

## Smart Contract Development
1. All smart contracts must be written in Motoko or Rust
2. Unit tests must cover at least 90% of the codebase
3. Integration tests must be performed before deployment
4. Gas optimization must be considered in all contract development

## Wallet Integration
1. Support for Internet Identity (II) is mandatory
2. Support for plug wallet is recommended
3. All wallet interactions must be clearly documented
4. Wallet connection must be persistent across sessions

## Transaction Handling
1. All transactions must include proper error handling
2. Transaction status must be clearly displayed to users
3. Failed transactions must be properly handled and reported
4. Transaction fees must be clearly communicated

## Compliance
1. KYC/AML procedures must be followed where required
2. All regulatory requirements must be met
3. User data must be handled according to privacy laws
4. Regular compliance audits must be conducted

## Documentation
1. All crypto-related features must be documented
2. API endpoints must be clearly documented
3. Smart contract interfaces must be documented
4. Security measures must be documented

## Testing
1. All crypto-related features must be tested in a testnet environment first
2. Load testing must be performed before mainnet deployment
3. Security testing must be performed regularly
4. Integration testing with wallets must be performed